          ]
        }
      },
      "disposition": {
        "reason": "All five findings reduce to two already-shipped, evidence-reviewed detector decisions, not a detector defect. The three bearer-token-header twins mutate a byte that still leaves both sides of a 40-byte value at or above MIN_TOKEN_LEN (16), so no single mid-value mutation at this index can produce a negative under the documented floor; the twin's chosen mutation index is untenable given that already-tested contract. The sendgrid base62-bearer-twin is correctly declined by sendgrid-token's own exact-length contract but is separately, correctly co-detected by bearer-token as a generic Bearer credential (67 bytes, well over the 16-byte floor) -- expected co-detection, not a discrimination failure. base62-generic-key-twin is a mainline generic-token true positive under the standing decision docs/decisions/2026-09-20-warn-unconditionally-on-high-signal-contextual-names.md (api_key= is a HIGH_SIGNAL_NAMES match, warned on unconditionally). Correcting the three benchmark fixtures (moving the bearer-token-header twin's mutation within 16 bytes of either edge; rescoping the two sendgrid twins to expect co-detection) is redact-secret-benchmarks follow-up work, not filed as of this record.",
